    "q-35272": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35272",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, \n$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]})=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
